<title>SOUTH KOREA: LG Cable wins $84 mln order for Israel power cable.</title>
<headline>LG Cable wins $84 mln order for Israel power cable.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's LG Cable and Machinery has won an $83 million order for power cables from the Israel Electric Corp Ltd, a company spokesman said on Monday.  </p>
<p>The spokesman said LG Cable and LG International Corp will jointly supply the 161 kilovolt (Kv) power cables and provide services to Israel Electric from October until June 1998.</p>
<p>Three hundred kilometres of cable will be installed in Tel Aviv, Haifa, Jerusalem and Negav, he said.</p>
<p>LG Cable expects 35 percent more orders from Israel Electric after completing the installation of the underground cables.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
